267
00:15:53,880 --> 00:15:55,420
We tried all sorts of things, didn't we.

268
00:15:55,420 --> 00:15:58,400
Digging pitfalls, setting up traps.

269
00:15:58,400 --> 00:16:02,460
Once Horamoya became the shopping district chairman,
he built machines and things.

270
00:16:02,460 --> 00:16:04,500
But in the end, it all failed.

271
00:16:04,500 --> 00:16:06,000
It's really laughable, isn't it.

272
00:16:06,000 --> 00:16:06,980
Thank you for waiting.

273
00:16:10,040 --> 00:16:12,620
So we don't have to do
that kind of thing anymore

274
00:16:16,500 --> 00:16:17,840
Isn't that a good thing?

275
00:16:18,360 --> 00:16:19,200
It's not good.

276
00:16:20,120 --> 00:16:23,540
Collecting Ryo-san's debts
was my reason for living.

277
00:16:23,940 --> 00:16:27,380
It's infuriating to hand
that over to those guys.

278
00:16:27,820 --> 00:16:28,460
Monk.

279
00:16:30,500 --> 00:16:32,100
My killer move...

280
00:16:32,940 --> 00:16:34,680
What on earth are you saying?

281
00:16:38,480 --> 00:16:40,120
Debt collection.

282
00:16:42,160 --> 00:16:43,320
You again?

283
00:16:43,320 --> 00:16:46,720
I told you I'd chase
you to the ends of hell.

284
00:16:46,720 --> 00:16:47,740
What will it take?

285
00:16:52,580 --> 00:16:53,680
What did you do?

286
00:16:53,680 --> 00:16:56,240
It's a special instant superglue.

287
00:16:56,240 --> 00:16:57,780
Tracking him is hopeless.

288
00:16:58,280 --> 00:16:59,260
Don't underestimate me.

289
00:17:00,820 --> 00:17:03,320
Full power!

290
00:17:11,240 --> 00:17:12,660
What a mess!

291
00:17:14,240 --> 00:17:16,320
Don't you dare come back!

292
00:17:17,560 --> 00:17:20,560
It seems I'll have to go myself.

293
00:17:20,560 --> 00:17:21,200
Sensei

294
00:17:21,980 --> 00:17:22,380
It's fine.

295
00:17:22,920 --> 00:17:25,020
I won't betray your expectations.

296
00:17:25,500 --> 00:17:26,920
Pleased to meet you.

297
00:17:33,620 --> 00:17:34,720
Is that all?

298
00:17:40,120 --> 00:17:41,660
H-he's good!

299
00:17:47,380 --> 00:17:50,600
So you managed to shake
off my subordinate's pursuit.

300
00:17:50,600 --> 00:17:53,580
You must be the boss of the debt collectors.

301
00:17:53,580 --> 00:17:56,100
My name is Mu, the Debt Collector.

302
00:17:56,100 --> 00:17:58,720
I'm a man who truly hates debt.

303
00:17:58,720 --> 00:17:59,520
What did you say?

304
00:18:00,040 --> 00:18:03,720
My parents ran a small shop in Hokkaido.

305
00:18:03,720 --> 00:18:08,160
But because of customers who never paid their tabs,
the shop went under.

306
00:18:08,160 --> 00:18:12,020
From that day on, I swore to myself

307
00:18:12,020 --> 00:18:15,180
that I would never let anyone get
away with skipping out on a debt.

308
00:18:16,320 --> 00:18:17,280
Give back my 100-yen shop!

309
00:18:26,520 --> 00:18:27,880
A UFO!

310
00:18:29,920 --> 00:18:30,640
Now!

311
00:18:35,000 --> 00:18:35,920
That's cheating!

312
00:18:36,060 --> 00:18:38,820
Normally,
a boss character fights alone, you know!

313
00:18:39,260 --> 00:18:43,060
I won't be called a coward by someone
who never returned a 100-yen item!

314
00:18:45,340 --> 00:18:46,460
It's the model shop guy.

315
00:18:48,300 --> 00:18:49,100
Hello?

316
00:18:51,920 --> 00:18:54,280
So they caught Ryo-san

317
00:18:59,120 --> 00:19:00,460
Ryo-san...

318
00:19:01,020 --> 00:19:03,080
Wow, well done!

319
00:19:03,480 --> 00:19:03,840
Thank you very much.

320
00:19:04,740 --> 00:19:06,440
You lot, I've misjudged you.

321
00:19:06,860 --> 00:19:09,700
Borrowing money from a bunch of
nonsensical people like these...

322
00:19:10,360 --> 00:19:12,120
Aren't you ashamed?

323
00:19:12,120 --> 00:19:13,420
So that's your side, then?

324
00:19:13,420 --> 00:19:17,320
Aren't you ashamed of
never paying back your debts?

325
00:19:18,320 --> 00:19:20,180
I'll pay back the debt someday.

326
00:19:21,680 --> 00:19:26,920
I'd rather die than that!
Don't worry, leave this child to me.

327
00:19:27,480 --> 00:19:33,240
Planning another cowardly trick? I'll show
you the true power of my boss character!

328
00:19:34,780 --> 00:19:38,120
Ugh... ugh...

329
00:19:38,120 --> 00:19:45,460
Now, you will want to repay your debts. You
will want to repay your debts. Sign, gelz.

330
00:19:46,520 --> 00:19:49,140
Damn it,
who would fall for hypnosis like that?

331
00:19:49,140 --> 00:19:53,180
It's useless.
You're already willing to pay your debts.

332
00:19:53,180 --> 00:19:55,840
You can't wait to pay off your debts.

333
00:19:55,840 --> 00:19:58,820
No matter what happens,
you'll pay your debts.

334
00:19:58,820 --> 00:20:04,180
You have debts, don't you?

335
00:20:04,180 --> 00:20:04,640
Yes.

336
00:20:04,640 --> 00:20:07,500
You have to repay your debts, don't you?

337
00:20:07,500 --> 00:20:08,500
Of course.

338
00:20:08,500 --> 00:20:12,380
Now, when I count to three, you will wake up

339
00:20:12,380 --> 00:20:14,200
and go repay your debts.

340
00:20:15,460 --> 00:20:15,700
3

341
00:20:16,920 --> 00:20:17,360
That's right.

342
00:20:17,960 --> 00:20:20,680
I have to pay back my debts.

343
00:20:20,680 --> 00:20:23,220
After borrowing money
left and right until now,

344
00:20:23,220 --> 00:20:25,020
I never paid a single yen back.

345
00:20:25,020 --> 00:20:27,680
What a terrible man I've been!

346
00:20:27,680 --> 00:20:30,160
Alright, starting now,
I'm paying back my debts!

347
00:20:31,500 --> 00:20:34,120
I've borrowed hundreds of millions until now,
after all.

348
00:20:34,660 --> 00:20:36,180
To that Nakagawa guy,

349
00:20:36,700 --> 00:20:40,000
I'm paying back this entire bonus to you,
Nakagawa!

350
00:20:40,000 --> 00:20:43,800
What's going on here?

351
00:20:45,460 --> 00:20:49,080
I think he went to repay
the biggest debt first, but

352
00:20:49,700 --> 00:20:53,660
so does that mean our debts won't come back?

353
00:20:53,660 --> 00:20:54,660
T-that's...

354
00:20:54,660 --> 00:20:55,780
You've got to be kidding.

355
00:20:55,780 --> 00:20:58,180
We're the ones who hired you.

356
00:20:58,180 --> 00:21:01,620
Take responsibility and collect our debts.

357
00:21:01,620 --> 00:21:02,540
I-I know.

358
00:21:02,540 --> 00:21:04,500
Bring him back right away.

359
00:21:06,560 --> 00:21:07,860
Pay back your debts!

360
00:21:07,860 --> 00:21:08,900
Let go!

361
00:21:08,900 --> 00:21:11,140
I'm going to go repay my debts.

362
00:21:11,140 --> 00:21:11,340
Dee!

363
00:21:12,380 --> 00:21:15,240
Don't you dare get in the
way of my debt repayment!

364
00:21:15,980 --> 00:21:17,200
I'm the winner here!

365
00:21:17,500 --> 00:21:19,340
I'm absolutely going to repay my debts!

366
00:21:20,320 --> 00:21:20,880
Nakagawa!

367
00:21:27,300 --> 00:21:28,720
Oh no, this is terrible.

368
00:21:28,720 --> 00:21:31,060
I knew it would turn out like this.

369
00:21:31,860 --> 00:21:34,300
People who don't really know Ryo-san

370
00:21:34,300 --> 00:21:36,860
couldn't possibly collect a debt from him,
could they?

371
00:21:37,400 --> 00:21:39,940
Hiring people like that was a mistake.

372
00:21:41,140 --> 00:21:43,240
If we do it ourselves, the cost will be

373
00:21:43,240 --> 00:21:44,920
So what if it is?

374
00:21:44,920 --> 00:21:47,600
Who cares how much money it costs?

375
00:21:48,760 --> 00:21:51,340
The reason we chase after
mass production every year

376
00:21:51,340 --> 00:21:52,900
isn't just for the money.

377
00:21:52,900 --> 00:21:56,100
It's a matter of pride for
people who run a business.

378
00:21:56,620 --> 00:21:57,340
Pride?

379
00:21:57,980 --> 00:22:00,520
We make sure to collect
payment for the goods we sell.

380
00:22:00,520 --> 00:22:02,680
No matter how much trouble it takes.

381
00:22:02,680 --> 00:22:05,700
Isn't that what a merchant's pride is?

382
00:22:05,700 --> 00:22:06,260
Yeah.

383
00:22:06,660 --> 00:22:08,520
That's a good point, Ma-san.

384
00:22:08,520 --> 00:22:10,160
A merchant's pride

385
00:22:11,140 --> 00:22:13,260
Well, it seems we were wrong.

386
00:22:13,260 --> 00:22:14,600
Yeah, Tenki-ya-san!

387
00:22:14,840 --> 00:22:18,320
B-but what about this year's bonus scramble?

388
00:22:18,540 --> 00:22:20,040
Are we giving up already?

389
00:22:20,500 --> 00:22:21,035
It's simple.

390
00:22:21,085 --> 00:22:25,040
There's a method only people
who know Ryo-san well can use.

391
00:22:26,580 --> 00:22:29,380
Nakagawa! I'm paying you back right now!

392
00:22:34,300 --> 00:22:37,760
There's money lying around here!

393
00:22:41,160 --> 00:22:43,800
What? What am I doing in a place like this?

394
00:22:44,060 --> 00:22:46,680
I'm pretty sure I was caught
by the debt collectors, though.

395
00:22:46,680 --> 00:22:49,680
Never mind that,
I just heard the sound of a bell falling -

396
00:22:49,680 --> 00:22:52,220
Where? Where?

397
00:22:54,120 --> 00:22:56,060
Didn't I just hear the senpai's voice -

398
00:22:56,860 --> 00:23:00,160
Found it! Yes! Lucky!

399
00:23:00,600 --> 00:23:02,560
Whoa! Damn, it was a trap!

400
00:23:02,820 --> 00:23:04,560
There, see? That's all it takes.

401
00:23:05,940 --> 00:23:08,780
Alright, Ryo-san,
you're going to pay back your debts.

402
00:23:09,780 --> 00:23:39,060
Mmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmm

403
00:23:39,780 --> 00:23:43,660
We'll collect those debts ourselves,
no matter what!

404
00:23:44,160 --> 00:23:44,820
Ooh!

405
00:23:51,300 --> 00:23:52,160
What should I do?

406
00:23:52,160 --> 00:23:55,040
After eating a weird fruit
that drifted in from the sea,

407
00:23:55,040 --> 00:23:58,080
I turned into a rubber man
whose body stretches like rubber.

408
00:23:58,560 --> 00:23:59,260
Wait.

409
00:23:59,260 --> 00:24:00,960
My arms and legs go byooon and stretch out!

410
00:24:00,960 --> 00:24:03,160
Actually, this could come in handy.

411
00:24:03,620 --> 00:24:05,660
Next time: mass production of Gomu Gomu!

412
00:24:06,040 --> 00:24:06,740
Stay tuned, okay?

413
00:24:11,680 --> 00:24:13,800
Well, you're sure to find Kame-ari!

414
00:24:14,800 --> 00:24:19,080
Everyone, come visit our town!

415
00:24:19,960 --> 00:24:20,680
Thank you!

